user: Please help me implement the full `docs/proposals/agent-runner-markdown-transcripts.md` proposal. Use JSON manifest plus `.md` bodies. My objection to JSON was not as a manifest format, which does not have the same readability restrictions as the Markdown bodies. Do not restrict sizes or number of entries. Follow the proposed storage layout and manifest schema. Note that a block may be very long and the user needs to always see what is going on, as it happens. Therefore we need to work with content that may be temporarily truncated while it gets live updates.
Do not use j/k for up/down; But support page-up/down keys. Otherwise, as suggested in the document.
I agree about continuing an old session, as a new "Continue as a new session" with only user prompts and final assistant answers, but also include a link to the session, in case the assistant want to look up something, but tell it the size of the session, so that it knows not to read everything. Only offer this capability to continue for the new style augmented session capture. In fact once this lands we don't need to support the old format at all. It's enough with just the new one.
We'll start working with current dependencies, as much as possible and defer investigating alternatives for now. Let us see how far this takes us first, then we can decide if further investigations are warranted and worhtwhile.
Please going until yuo implemented all parts, but commit each part separately. Take care to make this an efficient and complete implementation with full testing. Thanks

