Design decisions to nail down before coding:

### Manifest schema (JSON)

```json
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "agent-runner-conversation",
  "session_id": "session-2026-10-06T16-00-00Z-example",
  "canonical_evidence": false,
  "status": "running" | "completed" | "cancelled" | "failed" | "interrupted",
  "markdown_profile": "commonmark-gfm-subset-v1",
  "created_at": "2026-10-06T16:00:00Z",
  "finished_at": null,
  "parent_session": null | "session-...",
  "imported_from": null | { "session": "session-...", "messages": ["message-000003", ...] },
  "turns": 3, "tokens": null|1234, "tools": 2,
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "message-000001",
      "sequence": 1,
      "prompt": 1,
      "kind": "user" | "assistant" | "reasoning" | "tool" | "system",
      "disposition": null | "final" | "intermediate" | "truncated",
      "media_type": "text/markdown" | "text/plain",
      "path": "messages/000001.md",
      "bytes": 31,
      "sha256": "sha256:...",
      "complete": true,
      "truncated": false,
      "turn": 1,
      "tool_call": null | { "name": "shell", "call_id": "call_1", "failed": false }
    }
  ]
}
```

The proposal's example has: id, sequence, prompt, kind, disposition (assistant), media_type, path, bytes, complete, truncated. I'll add sha256 (digest — the proposal says "digests detect inconsistency"), created/finished_at timestamps, and tool linkage. Keep it tight.

Status values: the proposal says status: completed. For a live session: "running". On end: completed/failed/cancelled/interrupted (crash). Definition:
- running — session in progress (manifest published with this status; entries added as they complete)
- completed — all prompts completed normally
- cancelled — user cancelled
- failed — an error
- interrupted — process died (detected at load time: status was running at last write, or an entry is incomplete)

Entry kinds:
- user — user prompt (text/markdown)
- assistant — assistant text (text/markdown), disposition is final|intermediate
- reasoning — provider reasoning (text/markdown), only when provided and recording enabled
- tool — tool result, literal text (text/plain) — "tool results are literal text... not automatically interpreted as Markdown"
- note? — host notices? The journal already holds operational metadata. Keep notes out of the conversation record (journal's territory). Actually, the proposal says "trusted host-generated tool summaries can be separate Markdown entries" — tool results are literal text; fine.

Entry IDs: message-NNNNNN (6 digits), sequence = position in entries array, prompt = prompt index (1-based).

