The log directory is `.agent-runner/runs`. Currently: `session-<stamp>-<slug>.log` + `.jsonl`. New: directory `session-<stamp>-<slug>/` containing `session.json`, `messages/NNNNNN.md`. The `.jsonl` journal stays (operational, hashes only) — the proposal says to keep the journal. Where to put the journal? Currently next to .log in the log directory. To keep the conversation directory as the single session unit, I could put the journal inside the session directory as `journal.jsonl`. That's cleaner: everything for one session in one directory. The proposal's layout shows only session.yaml/messages/attachments, but the journal is "the existing operational journal" — the proposal says "the journal and conversation records are kept purpose-specific and avoid duplication of authoritative body text." Moving journal.jsonl into the session directory is a good move and I think consistent. Keep the name as `journal.jsonl`.

